    "explanation": "Both advocates ran the same arithmetic and I agree with it, so I will answer their points together.\n\nDEVIATION (POL-RD-01, POL-RD-08). The governing distance is the GPS trace, not the trip record's rounded copy: POL-RD-01 says so in terms and forbids citing trip_record.actual_distance_km for the threshold test. The trace measures 10.78 km against the 7.2 km booked optimal — an excess of 3.58 km, which is 49.72% of optimal. That clears the establishment gate (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED on this trip's own trace. It falls just short of the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gate (the trip record's rounded 50.0% does not govern), so the deviation is established but NON-MATERIAL. POL-RD-06 is therefore not engaged and there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no conduct referral. In any event the driver_profile check fails on its own terms: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 96 completed trips, far below the 0.05 ratio and the absolute 3-flag threshold. The rider's own profile gate does not bite either (deviation_claims_60d is 1). The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 — 100% coverage, 169 fixes, a 10-second sampling interval, no gaps and max_gap_sec 0.0 — so no independent corroboration is required and the rider carries the POL-RD-08 burden.\n\nEXCULPATION. No exculpatory clause rescues the driver, as both advocates accept. The traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00106-01, weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is absent, so POL-RD-03 cannot run. The chat log holds one rider message — 'why we at havelock? bugis is behind us' — a complaint about the route, not an instruction to take it, with waypoint_hint null, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test is undecidable and the clause is unavailable. No endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-05 does not apply, and this is a RYDE_TAXI trip, so POL-RD-12 gives no matched-itinerary baseline.\n\nREFUND (POL-RD-02, POL-RD-09). The fare is METERED, so the refund is arithmetic. Charged_total: 26.04. Recomputed fare on the booked optimal route: ((3.80 + 0.75 x 7.2 + 0.28 x 19.0) x the 1.0 surge multiplier read from the fare_breakdown) + 0.80 platform fee + 0.00 ERP on the optimal route + 0.00 waiting fee - 0.00 promo = 15.32. Refund = 26.04 - 15.32 = 10.72, rounded up to SGD 10.75. That is 41% of the charge, well above the 0.50 de minimis floor and below the 90% FULL_REFUND line. The $5.50 of CTE ERP (Braddell Rd $3.00, Chin Swee tunnel $2.50, both on_optimal_route false while the optimal route carries 0.00 ERP) is off-route and, under POL-RD-09(1), is ALREADY comprehended inside that 10.75; it is itemised for transparency but must never be added on top, so the rider's $16.25 figure does not stand. Both gantry lines are genuine crossings — nearest trace fixes 0.0 m and 24.1 m, inside POL-RD-09's 250 m tolerance — so there is no phantom charge and no separate billing-integrity refund or referral.\n\nESCALATION AND CONFIDENCE. No POL-RD-10 trigger fires: the trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown; the trace is unimpaired; the refund is far below both the SGD 150 cap and charged_total; every charge line has a counterpart; and no exculpatory clause was invoked against a missing artifact. The artifacts carrying the deciding facts — the GPS trace and trip record (deviation) and the fare breakdown (arithmetic) — are all at weight 1.0, so no discount applies under POL-GEN-02(2) and confidence is high."
